  "page1": {
    "title": "Every Life Counts",
    "subtitle": "A person, an animal, a tiny bug — each one wants to live.",
    "body": "Look at the people around you. Every life is special. A person, a dog, and a small bug all want to live. We call this respect for life.\n\nIt means we care for every living thing. We should not hurt others for fun. We should be kind and gentle.\n\nWhen a friend is sad, we help. When a plant is dry, we give it water. These small acts <mark>show that we care</mark>.\n\nCaring for life is also a duty. Each of us has this duty every day. We keep weak and small things safe.\n\nA safe world begins with one kind heart. Today, choose to protect life.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/19.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A child waters a dry plant while a small dog and a tiny bug rest nearby — every life cared for.",
    "glossary": [
      {
        "term": "respect for life",
        "ko": "생명 존중 (모든 생명을 소중히 여김)"
      }
    ]
  },
